.Dd October 6, 2026
.Dt BHOTKEYS-GREETER 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm bhotkeys-greeter
.Nd start and stop the login greeter listener
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm start
.Nm
.Cm stop
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
starts the greeter listener and stops it before the user
session takes the display.
The listener is
.Nm bhotkeys Fl Fl daemon Fl Fl greeter .
It does not share a process with the session listener.
.Pp
.Cm start
also starts a system
.Xr pulseaudio 1
instance when that program is installed, so volume keys
have a server before a user session exists, and runs
.Xr bosd-start 1
when it is on
.Ev PATH .
The PulseAudio daemon is started as root with
.Fl Fl system
and drops to user
.Sy pulse .
.Cm stop
stops the listener, that PulseAudio instance, and the
.Xr bosd 1
daemon of the uid that ran
.Cm start .
Display managers run these hooks as root, so that daemon
is the greeter's, not the session user's.
.Pp
.Cm start
and
.Cm stop
exit 0.
A missing program is logged and skipped.
GDM aborts the login when
.Pa PostLogin/Default
exits non-zero, and
.Xr pam_exec 8
without
.Cm optional
turns a non-zero status into a failed session.
.Pp
The listener runs as root.
Commands it runs are found on
.Ev PATH .
.Nm
puts
.Pa @PREFIX@/bin
on that path.
.Ev HOME
for those commands is
.Pa /root .
.Pp
User
.Sy pulse
must be in group
.Sy audio
or the OSS sinks do not open.
.Nm
does not change group membership.
.Pp
XDM and GDM each run a root script before the greeter and
another when the user session is about to start.
SDDM runs a root script before the greeter and has no root
script at the handoff.
The session PAM stack is root, and that is the stop.
Do not use an XDG autostart entry for this.
The greeter is not a user session.
GDM's
.Pa greeter/autostart
directory runs as user
.Sy gdm ,
which is the wrong user for this listener.
.Ss XDM
.Pa Xsetup
runs as root after the server accepts connections.
.Pa GiveConsole
runs as root before the session.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# Xsetup
\&. @PREFIX@/share/examples/bhotkeys/xdm/Xsetup

# GiveConsole
\&. @PREFIX@/share/examples/bhotkeys/xdm/GiveConsole
.Ed
.Ss GDM
.Pa Init/Default
runs as root after the server starts and before the
greeter.
GDM waits for it.
.Pa PostLogin/Default
runs as root after authentication and before
.Fn pam_open_session .
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# Init/Default
\&. @PREFIX@/share/examples/bhotkeys/gdm/Init

# PostLogin/Default
\&. @PREFIX@/share/examples/bhotkeys/gdm/PostLogin
.Ed
.Ss SDDM
The X11
.Va DisplayCommand
.Pq Pa Xsetup
runs as root before the greeter.
Add the line in
.Pa @PREFIX@/share/examples/bhotkeys/sddm/pam
to the session group of
.Pa pam.d/sddm
and of
.Pa pam.d/sddm-autologin .
Leave
.Pa pam.d/sddm-greeter
alone.
That stack is the greeter itself.
.Xr pam_exec 8
runs
.Nm stop
as root when the user session opens, and again when it
closes.
.Pa Xstop
runs when the X server exits.
On X11 that is logout, not the handoff.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "PULSE_SERVER"
.It Ev DISPLAY
X server.
The default is
.Pa :0 .
.It Ev XAUTHORITY
Cookie file.
When it is unset or unreadable,
.Nm
uses the XDM auth file for this display under
.Pa /var/db/xdm/authdir/authfiles
when one is readable.
.It Ev PULSE_SERVER
PulseAudio socket.
The default is
.Pa unix:/var/run/pulse/native .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "@PREFIX@/share/bhotkeys/greeter-system.pa"
.It Pa @PREFIX@/share/bhotkeys/greeter-system.pa
Script for the system PulseAudio instance.
.It Pa @PREFIX@/share/examples/bhotkeys/
Snippets for XDM, GDM, and SDDM.
.It Pa /var/run/bhotkeys-greeter.pid
Listener pid.
.It Pa /var/run/pulse/pid
System PulseAudio pid.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 1 when the arguments are wrong, and 0 otherwise.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bhotkeys 1 ,
.Xr bhotkeys-start 1 ,
.Xr bosd 1 ,
.Xr bosd-start 1 ,
.Xr pulseaudio 1 ,
.Xr pam_exec 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Devin Teske Aq Mt dteske@FreeBSD.org
